---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="404">
  <section class="prose not-found">
    <h1>404 - Page not found (in this model)</h1>
   <!-- <p>
      Assume the page exists, derive <code>⊥</code>, conclude <code>I'm a teapot</code>.
    </p>
-->

    <p>
      The good news: by non-constructive existence, the page may exist.
      The bad news: we failed to construct a witness.
    </p>
<!--
    <details>
      <summary>Proof sketch (click to expand)</summary>
      <pre><code>Goal: FindPage(url)

1. Reduce FindPage(url) to HALT(program(url))
2. Observe: HALT is undecidable
3. Therefore: the existence of this page is… complicated
4. Return 404 (sound, but probably incomplete)</code></pre>
    </details>
-->

<!--
    <p>
      If you’re a type theorist: this route’s type appears to be uninhabited.
      If you’re a logician: it might be independent of our routing axioms.
      If you’re a complexity theorist: we can approximate it within 404 ± ε.
    </p>
--> 
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/">Return to home</a>
      <!-- <a href="/sitemap.xml">Consult the oracle (sitemap)</a> -->
    </p>

    <p class="fineprint">
      Tip: if you believe the page exists, please provide either (a) a URL,
      (b) a constructive proof, or (c) a pull request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .not-found {
      max-width: 44rem;
    }

    .actions {
      margin-top: 1.75rem;
    }

    details {
      margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      background: var(--color-surface);
    }

    pre {
      margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
      overflow-x: auto;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      background: #f7f4ee;
    }

    .fineprint {
      margin-top: 2rem;
      opacity: 0.8;
      font-size: 0.95em;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
